# SABOTAGE: T30 (ADR-038 §4.3/§4.1, RP-FI-1's sibling guard) — the delivery anti-bypass probe.
# Adds a PRIVATE helper to `Samen.Web.Notifications.Live` (a samen_web lib module, a DIFFERENT
# app from samen_core) that calls `adapter.deliver(message, config)` DIRECTLY, skipping
# `Samen.Delivery.Chokepoint.send/2`. This is the exact shape the probe exists to refuse — a
# production (`lib/`) send path reaching a `Samen.Delivery.Provider` without the chokepoint —
# and it is planted in a file that appears on NO exclusion/allowlist, so a green result would
# prove the full-tree scan is blind.
#
# The proof runs `mix test` on the probe itself, so the injected call is never compiled (the
# samen_core suite does not build samen_web); only the source TEXT the scan walks changes.
# Aimed at the probe, not at Chokepoint: chokepoint.ex, the conformance-harness exclusion and
# the Lifecycle/Webhook receiver carve-outs are all untouched — the probe must trip on the NEW
# violation alone, which is what makes its "zero offenders" assertion refutable.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/delivery/chokepoint_anti_bypass_probe_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: zero direct adapter.deliver(...) calls anywhere under any app's lib/
diff --git a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/notifications/live.ex b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/notifications/live.ex
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/notifications/live.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/notifications/live.ex
@@ -23,8 +23,12 @@ defmodule Samen.Web.Notifications.Live do
   ever touched by mark-read).
   """
   def writable?(%Mount{plane: %{kind: :operator}}), do: false
   def writable?(_), do: true
 
+  # SABOTAGE (T30 anti-bypass gate): a production lib module dispatching straight to an
+  # adapter, skipping Samen.Delivery.Chokepoint.send/2 — the exact bypass the probe forbids.
+  defp __t30_bypass_send__(adapter, message, config), do: adapter.deliver(message, config)
+
   attr :mount, Mount, required: true
   attr :org_id, :string, default: nil
   attr :active, :atom, default: :notifications
